# Elite Architecture Guardrails

- `apps/desktop` is the only desktop frontend. Do not add a separate frontend runtime under `apps/desktop-backend`.
- `apps/desktop-backend` owns native command/domain/persistence logic only.
- Reject dead scaffold artifacts and duplicate entrypoints (unused HTML/Vite shells, orphan scripts, stale config).
- Preserve strict 3-app boundaries:
  - `desktop`: product UX + command adapters
  - `desktop-backend`: Tauri/Rust engine
  - `web`: marketing/sales/docs/download only
- If a change introduces architectural ambiguity, stop and enforce the canonical boundary before adding features.
